hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27329","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, from his father, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from his grandmother Rumaytha, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If I wished to kiss the seal between his shoulders because of my closeness to him, I would do so. He says: The Throne of the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted, shook, meaning Sad ibn Muadh, on the day he died."
"27330","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada al-Zafari, from his grandmother Rumaytha, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
